Subject: [PATCH] The follower up stairs and into caves with the player (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The follower went into its ball whenever the player went up or down
stairs or into a cave or a forest (the game walks the player there: "the
game moves the player"), and came out again only once the player stood
still, its ball first. Now it goes with them, as HeartGold's does:
during such a warp's way in or out (the task sub_02056BDC and
sub_02056C18 start: FieldSystem_PortWarpKind) it isn't put away, and on
the other side it's out at once without its ball, behind the player or,
on their tile (the stairs'), shown once they've stepped off it. Through
a building's door (in by it, transition 1; out onto it) it goes into
its ball and comes out of it, as before. When it's in its ball and the
player sets off walking, it comes out behind them as they go, growing
out of nothing, instead of waiting for them to stop (its ball, as
before, when they stand). And going into its ball, it waits a few frames
for room for its ball's picture: handing the party to the nurse, the
player's own picture changes in the same frame, and the Pokémon went in
with no ball.
